course: dictionary
lesson: 14221
title: Mutual: shared by both
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mutual means something that goes both ways. «Sam and Priya have mutual respect.» Sam respects Priya, and Priya respects Sam. The respect is felt by each of them towards the other.
explain: Mutual can also mean shared by two or more people. «We met through a mutual friend.» The friend knows both of you, so the friend is shared between you. Ask yourself: does the feeling or the thing go both ways, or is it shared?
explain: Mutual is often used in phrases. «The feeling is mutual» means I feel the same about you. «Both teams signed a mutual agreement» means both sides agreed. When you meet mutual, swap in «both» or «shared» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Mutual means felt or done by each of two or more people towards the other.
fact: Mutual also means shared by two or more people.
fact: «Mutual respect» means each person respects the other.
fact: «The feeling is mutual» means I feel the same about you.
fact: Mutual is an adjective, and its adverb is mutually.
exercise: «The two friends have mutual trust.» What does mutual mean here? | Very loud | Lost and found | *Felt by each of them towards the other | Felt by only one of them
exercise: «We met through a mutual friend.» What does mutual mean here? | Unkind | Very old | *Shared by both of us | Hidden under a bed
exercise: «Both teams signed a mutual agreement.» Which phrase means the same as mutual here? | *Agreed by both sides | Signed by one team only | Agreed by nobody | Written in red ink
test: «Mia and Omar have mutual respect for each other.» What does mutual respect mean? | Respect is lost | *Each one respects the other | Respect is for cars | Only Mia respects Omar
test: Adam says, «The feeling is mutual.» What does he mean? | *I feel the same about you | I am leaving now | I am not sure what I feel | I am angry with you
exam: Which word means shared by two or more people? | *Mutual | Single | Solo | Lonely
